  fit: {mode: fill}
notes: |
  Timing: about 60 seconds.

  My ready-made is called Tether. It is an ordinary nylon-braided charging cable that came with the Mac I began using at university. Within one year, both connectors had frayed. When I was younger, I could not understand why my mother's cables broke while mine stayed new. Now the positions have reversed because so much of my reading, work, and attention happens through a screen. By selecting and naming the cable, I treated its damage as evidence: the object had recorded my habits. Like a ready-made, its meaning came from recontextualization rather than fabrication.
